{title: Drunken Sailor}
{subtitle: Beginner arrangement - two chords in a minor key}
{artist: Traditional sea shanty}
{key: Am}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 120}
{tag: beginner, shanty, two chords, minor}
# Traditional words selected from The Shanty Book, Part I (1921), no. 14.
# Fresh two-chord accompaniment, not Terry's piano arrangement.
{comment: Strum DDDD}
{comment: Keep a steady pulse through Am and G. Start slowly; speed is optional.}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Am]What shall we do with the drunken sailor?
[G]What shall we do with the drunken sailor?
[Am]What shall we do with the drunken sailor,
[G]Early in the [Am]morning?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Am]Hooray and up she rises,
[G]Hooray and up she rises,
[Am]Hooray and up she rises,
[G]Early in the [Am]morning.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Am]Put him in the long-boat until he's sober,
[G]Put him in the long-boat until he's sober,
[Am]Put him in the long-boat until he's sober,
[G]Early in the [Am]morning.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Am]Hooray and up she rises,
[G]Hooray and up she rises,
[Am]Hooray and up she rises,
[G]Early in the [Am]morning.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Am]Pull out the plug and wet him all over,
[G]Pull out the plug and wet him all over,
[Am]Pull out the plug and wet him all over,
[G]Early in the [Am]morning.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Am]Hooray and up she rises,
[G]Hooray and up she rises,
[Am]Hooray and up she rises,
[G]Early in the [Am]morning.
{end_of_chorus}
